<h2>My Blog</h2>

As a professional software developer I created a blog in 2005 <a href="https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/archive/blogs/calvin_hsia/">Calvin’s Blog </a>
Originally, it was posted at blogs.msdn.com. Back in 2005, blogs were new and lots of people created blogs. I created a web site (in Visual FoxPro) used internally at Microsoft to show blog statistics once a month to see which blogs were most popular. Sort of a newer version of Calvin’s List (which earned me the position of one of the 1st Microsoft MVPs)
Over the years, people came and went from Microsoft, leaving their blogs abandoned.
Microsoft decided to retire blogs.msdn.com, but there was a lot of good content which was archived to docs.microsoft.com/archive
<br>
See also <a href="https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/archive/blogs/calvin_hsia/what-is-a-microsoft-mvp-calvins-list-updated-for-the-new-century">https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/archive/blogs/calvin_hsia/what-is-a-microsoft-mvp-calvins-list-updated-for-the-new-century</a>
